{
 "title": "LIF with an axonal delay",
 "description": "The LIF neuron with a Delay on its way out: the axon. The Delay holds each spike back a whole number of steps (3 here, set in its details), so a spike fired at step t leaves the layer at step t + 3 and whatever reads this layer hears it late. The reset still reads the neuron's own last spike straight away; only what travels down the axon is delayed. 1,024 parameters.",
